  "id": "COMPOUND:161 - PROTEIN:1655",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between adenosine triphosphate (ATP) and Heat shock cognate 71 kDa protein (HSP71), mediated through a series of molecular interactions involving a common target molecule. ATP is linked to multiple targets, including ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 11 (ABCC11), PAXF546, and DNA-directed RNA polymerase subunit beta'. These targets are all involved in processes that ultimately lead to the activation of HSP71. The shared pathway involves the binding of a specific compound, (3S,10S,13S)-17-[1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-N,N,10,13-tetramethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-amine, which acts as a modulator of these targets. This compound is implicated in regulating cellular processes, and its interaction with HSP71 suggests a possible role in stress response or protein homeostasis. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between ATP and HSP71, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
